## 2. Paid licenses

Except for ProntoCare (section 3), PhotoMed **is not free of charge**. Using, copying, installing, modifying,
distributing, sublicensing, selling or commercially exploiting the Software requires a **paid
license** issued in writing by the licensor (purchase order, invoice or contract). Without a valid
license there is no right of use.

### 2.1 License types

| License type | For whom | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| **Professional** | A healthcare or medical aesthetics professional | 1 user, up to 2 devices |
| **Clinic** | A center or practice | Users and devices at one site, according to the number contracted |
| **Institutional / network** | Groups, clinic networks, insurers and healthcare service companies | Multiple sites and users; terms set by contract |

### 2.2 Price and payment terms

- Each license type is contracted as a **subscription** (monthly or annual, renewable) or, at the
  licensor's option, as a **perpetual license for the version purchased** with an optional annual fee for
  updates and support.
- Prices are those of the licensor's **current price list** or those set in the purchase order or the
  contract, plus applicable taxes.
- Payment is in advance. If a subscription is not renewed or not paid, the license is suspended
  at the end of the paid period; the user's photographs and data remain the user's property and
  remain on the user's devices.
- Unless the law provides otherwise, amounts paid are non-refundable.
- Licenses and quotes: juanfrank11@gmail.com.

